{#
  ONE definition of a sub-page hero's responsive URLs, called by BOTH the <img>
  element and by head.njk's preload.

  This exists because the element's `srcset` and the preload's `imagesrcset`
  have to be byte-identical or the preload fetches a candidate the element never
  uses -- highest-priority bytes nothing draws, and the hero that DOES draw gets
  no preload at all. head.njk's own comment records that regression happening
  here on 2026-09-02, when a hand-written preload path and the field that
  rendered the background drifted apart. Written once and imported twice, they
  cannot disagree.

  `heroWidths` and `heroDims` are filters, not dictionary lookups, and they
  throw on a stem that is not in src/_data/heroVariants.json. See .eleventy.js.
#}

{%- macro heroSrcset(stem) -%}
{%- for w in stem | heroWidths -%}/img/{{ stem }}-{{ w }}w.webp {{ w }}w{% if not loop.last %}, {% endif %}{%- endfor -%}
{%- endmacro -%}

{%- macro heroLargest(stem) -%}
/img/{{ stem }}-{{ (stem | heroWidths) | last }}w.webp
{%- endmacro -%}

{#
  The hero itself. Doc 10 s2.3: text never sits on photography EXCEPT the
  sub-page hero <h1>, which sits on a bottom-third scrim, left-aligned at the
  gutter. s5.3 names the component and its 60svh height.

  `object-position` is NOT a parameter here. It is a per-page CSS override keyed
  off the page wrapper's existing id (see styles.css), because an inline
  `style=` attribute would need a CSP hash and the whole point of replacing the
  old `style="background-image: url(...)"` divs with an <img> was to leave CSP
  untouched -- and to carry alt text those divs never had.

  `.reveal` is on the CONTENT block only. The photograph is static and
  first-paint -- "it's a photograph, not a rig" (s5.3). No hold: heldTargets()
  in js/animations.js is page-home only and stays so.
#}
{%- macro heroSub(stem, alt, heading, subtitle) -%}
<section class="hero-sub">
    <img src="{{ heroLargest(stem) }}" srcset="{{ heroSrcset(stem) }}" sizes="100vw"
         alt="{{ alt }}" class="hero-sub__image"
         fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"
         width="{{ (stem | heroDims).w }}" height="{{ (stem | heroDims).h }}">
    <div class="hero-sub__content reveal">
        <h1>{{ heading }}</h1>
        <p>{{ subtitle }}</p>
    </div>
</section>
{%- endmacro -%}
